# BUBBLE DEFENSE — AGENT RULES (.cursorrules)

> Binding rules for every human or AI contributor. If a rule conflicts with a request,
> stop and flag the conflict in `docs/STATE_AND_TASKS.md` → "Open Questions".

---

## 0. Project Identity

- Product: **Bubble Defense** — a high-precision 2D physics arcade game.
- Stack: **100% Kotlin**, Jetpack Compose `Canvas` for rendering. No game engines, no
  OpenGL/Vulkan wrappers, no third-party physics libraries, no Java source files.
- Package root: `com.arcade.bubbledefense`.
- Units everywhere in simulation code: **world units (wu)**, **seconds (s)**, **radians**.
  World space is a virtual `1000 x 1800` wu rectangle, origin top-left, **+Y points DOWN**.
- Modular Rules & Skills Integration:
  - Rules: `.agents/rules/` (`01-zero-alloc-hot-loop`, `02-docs-and-tasks`, `03-compose-and-threading`, `04-physics-and-math`, `05-economy-quarantine`).
  - Skills: Active specialized architectural skills in `.agents/skills/` (and `.antigravity/skills/`):
    - `kinetic-flow-architect`: Flow state, dopamine clocks, juice matrix, sub-300ms retry.
    - `kotlin-ux-architect`: 120Hz Compose phase hygiene, zero-alloc Canvas, gesture sampling.
    - `arcade-economy-architect`: Flow-state monetization, procedural skins, SDK quarantine.

---

## 1. Docs-as-Memory, Master Tasklist & Versioning Protocol (MANDATORY)

`/docs` is the persistent state machine of this project. Code without matching docs is a bug.

### 1.1 Master Tasklist Discipline (`docs/STATE_AND_TASKS.md`)
- **Single Source of Truth:** `docs/STATE_AND_TASKS.md` contains the master tasklist for all phases.
- **Before writing any code:**
  1. Inspect `docs/STATE_AND_TASKS.md` to identify the active phase, current task, and handoff notes.
  2. Mark the target task as in-progress (`[/]`).
  3. Read the relevant architectural specs (`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `PHYSICS_SPEC.md`, `GAME_DESIGN.md`).
- **During & after code execution:**
  1. If any constant, equation, or pool layout changes, update the spec document first.
  2. Mark completed tasks (`[x]`).
  3. Record newly discovered edge cases in Section 3 of `STATE_AND_TASKS.md`.
  4. Write a dated handoff log for the next agent turn.
- Never merge or skip execution phases. Pause for user review at the end of each phase.

### 1.2 Semantic Versioning (SemVer 2.0.0)
The project strictly tracks release and milestone versions using `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`:
- **`MAJOR`**: Breaking architectural shifts or complete engine rewrites (e.g. `v1.0.0` shipping candidate).
- **`MINOR`**: Completion of a full milestone phase introducing new systems (e.g. `v0.1.0` -> `v0.2.0` on Phase 2 completion).
- **`PATCH`**: Bug fixes, performance optimizations, spec synchronization, and unit test additions.
- Always log version transitions in the Change Log of `docs/STATE_AND_TASKS.md`.

### 1.3 Conventional Commits & Documentation Quality
All commit messages, PR titles, and agent turn summaries MUST follow the Conventional Commits specification:
```text
<type>(<scope>): [<PERSONA>] <description> (vX.Y.Z)
```
- **Allowed Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `chore`.
- **Scopes:** `math`, `collision`, `pool`, `loop`, `input`, `physics`, `render`, `director`, `juice`, `economy`, `hud`.
- **Persona Tags:** `[ARCH-AGENT]`, `[PHYS-AGENT]`, `[JUICE-AGENT]`, `[ECON-AGENT]`.
- **Example:** `feat(loop): [ARCH-AGENT] implement 120Hz fixed accumulator loop with hit-stop (v0.2.0)`
- **Documentation Standards:** Every code symbol (class, value class, function, pool) must feature comprehensive KDoc stating units (wu, wu/s, rad), coordinate space (+Y down), and zero-alloc guarantees. Banned: placeholders (`// TODO`, `...`, stubs).

